      "content": "Conservative religious arguments against MAID often hinge on the belief that life is sacred and only God has the authority to end it. This perspective prioritizes divine will over individual autonomy, which can stifle medical progress and infringe on personal rights. In contrast, secular and liberal religious frameworks emphasize rationality, personal freedom, and the evolving understanding of ethics. They argue that individuals should have the right to make decisions about their own bodies and lives, including the choice to end suffering through MAID. By clinging to tradition and divine authority, conservative religious arguments can be seen as outdated and illogical, failing to adapt to contemporary ethical standards and human rights.",
      "source": "target",
